{"data": [{"author_id": "733647469305864195", "created_at": "2026-11-08T16:50:41.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119472686900675000"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "s2.q4cdn.com/470004039/file…", "end": 268, "expanded_url": "https://s2.q4cdn.com/470004039/files/doc_earnings/2026/q4/filing/10K-Q4-2026-as-filed.pdf", "start": 245, "unwound_url": "https://s2.q4cdn.com/470004039/files/doc_earnings/2026/q4/filing/10K-Q4-2026-as-filed.pdf", "url": "https://t.co/zRyfpluOua"}]}, "id": "2119472686900675000", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 119, "impression_count": 64495, "like_count": 446, "quote_count": 7, "reply_count": 24, "retweet_count": 70}, "text": "It seems clear that the CBO and others have underestimated the loss to the US Treasury from profit shifting to low tax jurisdictions.\n\nMicron's US (federal) tax on $100b in income?   ~ 250m\n\nApple's US tax on $160b in income?   ~ $12b\n\n1/ many\n\nhttps://t.co/zRyfpluOua", "url": "https://x.com/Brad_Setser/status/2119472686900675000"}, {"author_id": "702235316812275712", "created_at": "2026-11-08T16:20:31.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119465097949290746"], "id": "2119465097949290746", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3123, "like_count": 5, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "I was explaining candy corn to my 5.5 year old in a similar way to how “gruel” was explained to us by our middle school teacher while reading Oliver Twist", "url": "https://x.com/EconBerger/status/2119465097949290746"}, {"author_id": "48463418", "created_at": "2026-11-08T16:00:13.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119459990238900700"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 4, "start": 0, "tag": "OTD"}, {"end": 241, "start": 226, "tag": "PhysicsHistory"}], "mentions": [{"end": 199, "id": "16465385", "start": 188, "username": "NobelPrize"}], "urls": [{"description": "The Nobel Prize in Physics 1901 was awarded to Wilhelm Conrad Röntgen \"in recognition of the extraordinary services he has rendered by the discovery of the remarkable rays subsequently named after him\"", "display_url": "go.aps.org/3UI7TPU", "end": 224, "expanded_url": "https://go.aps.org/3UI7TPU", "images": [{"height": 328, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2119459991643893760/xvZJKTGX?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 496}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2119459991643893760/xvZJKTGX?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 201, "status": 200, "title": "Nobel Prize in Physics 1901", "unwound_url": "https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/physics/1901/summary/", "url": "https://t.co/s1cqPpq17k"}]}, "id": "2119459990238900700", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 3, "impression_count": 2413, "like_count": 25, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 8}, "text": "#OTD in 1895, Wilhelm Röntgen noticed that when he shielded his tube with heavy black cardboard, a screen nine feet away still glowed. He called the unknown rays \"X-rays.\"\n\nRead more from @NobelPrize: https://t.co/s1cqPpq17k\n\n#PhysicsHistory", "url": "https://x.com/APSphysics/status/2119459990238900700"}, {"author_id": "3512101", "created_at": "2026-11-08T15:57:19.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119459258077204718"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/45T9jkXhgJ", "end": 98, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/niubi/status/2119459258077204718/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2119459240808980480", "start": 75, "url": "https://t.co/45T9jkXhgJ"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/45T9jkXhgJ", "end": 98, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/niubi/status/2119459258077204718/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2119459240800620544", "start": 75, "url": "https://t.co/45T9jkXhgJ"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/45T9jkXhgJ", "end": 98, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/niubi/status/2119459258077204718/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2119459240838414336", "start": 75, "url": "https://t.co/45T9jkXhgJ"}, {"display_url": "x.com/niubi/status/2…", "end": 122, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/niubi/status/2119405349891649543", "start": 99, "url": "https://t.co/AVHlhrxCtt"}]}, "id": "2119459258077204718", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 4, "impression_count": 4565, "like_count": 32, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 2}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2119405349891649543", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "With classic cameos from Jon Cena, Tim Cook, Elon Musk and Mark Zuckerberg https://t.co/45T9jkXhgJ https://t.co/AVHlhrxCtt", "url": "https://x.com/niubi/status/2119459258077204718"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-11-08T15:09:34.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119447239810486714"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "A California program providing trust funds for foster youth is giving traumatized young people a chance to pursue their dreams.", "display_url": "calmatters.org/politics/2026/…", "end": 218, "expanded_url": "https://calmatters.org/politics/2026/04/billionaire-tax-labor-divided/b", "images": [{"height": 1333, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2119447246680850433/SnLnOSXl?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 2000}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2119447246680850433/SnLnOSXl?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 195, "status": 200, "title": "California foster youth and COVID orphans gaining a sense of hope from trust fund program", "unwound_url": "https://calmatters.org/commentary/2024/01/baby-bonds-foster-youth-hope/", "url": "https://t.co/4sTXp5TJXm"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/iISxMQ9EpE", "end": 242, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2119447239810486714/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2119447234953494528", "start": 219, "url": "https://t.co/iISxMQ9EpE"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/iISxMQ9EpE", "end": 242, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2119447239810486714/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2119447234974490624", "start": 219, "url": "https://t.co/iISxMQ9EpE"}, {"display_url": "x.com/thestalwart/st…", "end": 266, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/thestalwart/status/2119436219486449860", "start": 243, "url": "https://t.co/sy8g8ZIfRZ"}]}, "id": "2119447239810486714", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 27, "impression_count": 29219, "like_count": 145, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 15, "retweet_count": 7}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2119436219486449860", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Not sure if this is the full answer. But a number of progressive and/or labor groups weren’t excited about the CA wealth tax, because they perceived health care workers as the main beneficiaries https://t.co/4sTXp5TJXm https://t.co/iISxMQ9EpE https://t.co/sy8g8ZIfRZ", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2119447239810486714"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-11-08T14:46:24.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119441412827631787"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/I8odWsQAZ4", "end": 167, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2119441412827631787/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2119441408520011776", "start": 144, "url": "https://t.co/I8odWsQAZ4"}, {"display_url": "x.com/seansullivanny…", "end": 191, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/seansullivannyt/status/2119192989524447453", "start": 168, "url": "https://t.co/K0Tzc9A4Tt"}]}, "id": "2119441412827631787", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 7, "impression_count": 17661, "like_count": 65, "quote_count": 3, "reply_count": 7, "retweet_count": 2}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2119192989524447453", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Some interesting comments in this article, but unfortunately the only quote about culture war issues, came from a professor rather than a voter https://t.co/I8odWsQAZ4 https://t.co/K0Tzc9A4Tt", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2119441412827631787"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-11-08T14:25:46.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119436219486449860"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/julianflpol/st…", "end": 302, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/julianflpol/status/2119249739178733848", "start": 279, "url": "https://t.co/dqvRqLNnXQ"}]}, "id": "2119436219486449860", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 75, "impression_count": 183185, "like_count": 865, "quote_count": 24, "reply_count": 197, "retweet_count": 40}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2119249739178733848", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Why did the wealth tax get crushed in CA? Was it because it was badly written? Was there any version of it that could have passed?\n\nI’m not sure a state/level approach makes sense, given domestic capital mobility. But this thing where we only tax W2 earners isn’t a great trend. https://t.co/dqvRqLNnXQ", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2119436219486449860"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-11-08T14:07:50.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119431705677439455"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/thestalwart/st…", "end": 175, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/thestalwart/status/2116969238820794633", "start": 152, "url": "https://t.co/zsJfXpD5cr"}]}, "id": "2119431705677439455", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 9, "impression_count": 26198, "like_count": 298, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 19, "retweet_count": 7}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2116969238820794633", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "If you didn’t think the week after the election would be spent by Democrats arguing about the strength of AES’ victory with each other you are a moron. https://t.co/zsJfXpD5cr", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2119431705677439455"}, {"author_id": "3512101", "created_at": "2026-11-08T12:23:06.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119405349891649543"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/realsert8964/s…", "end": 97, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/realsert8964/status/2119291448285876292", "start": 74, "url": "https://t.co/NJzrO1Klax"}]}, "id": "2119405349891649543", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 40, "impression_count": 18401, "like_count": 97, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 4, "retweet_count": 14}, "refer